  <h2>How a gift-card redemption works</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Lower minimums.</b> Gift-card thresholds are often far below bank minimums, so smaller balances are not stranded.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Same verification.</b> First redemptions still require identity checks before the operator releases the prize.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Not cash.</b> A gift card is locked to a retailer or card network and cannot be deposited like a bank transfer.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Retailer fit.</b> Value depends on whether you would shop at the offered retailer anyway.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Gift card vs other rails</h2>
  <p>Gift cards trade flexibility for a low minimum: <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/bank-transfer/">bank transfer</a> is unrestricted cash but slower with higher thresholds, and <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/crypto/">cryptocurrency</a> settles fastest but needs wallet handling. Compare all three in the <a href="/guides/sweepstakes-casino-redemption-methods/">redemption methods guide</a> and the <a href="/research/sweepstakes-casino-redemption-times/">redemption-time research</a>.</p>

